-- retirement_accounts row using one of the 6 Class-F contribution
-- catalogue keys, linked to a specific parent retirement account using the
-- best available evidence: same user_id + same currency_code, and exactly
-- ONE candidate parent account existing for that user (a genuine balance-
-- style retirement item — industry_super/retail_super/smsf/etc., not
-- another contribution row). This is a real but comparatively weak
-- evidence bar for a LINK (retirement_accounts carries no institution/
-- account-number field to further disambiguate, unlike the
-- deterministic-duplicate MERGE bar in Spec 2 §54-57, which needs strong
-- multi-factor evidence because a wrong merge would hide real money —
-- linking to a plausible parent account has no such risk: it never changes
-- any total, only which account a contribution's own record display is
-- associated with). Rows with zero or multiple (ambiguous) candidate
-- parent accounts for their user are deliberately EXCLUDED below and
-- listed as a genuine data-quality gap in
